  "ingredients": [
    "24 ounce ground beef (80/20)",
    "1 tablespoon garlic powder",
    "1 tablespoon onion powder",
    "1/2 tablespoon cumin",
    "1/2 tablespoon chinese five-spice powder",
    "1/2 tablespoon cayenne pepper",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "2 tablespoon full-fat plain greek yogurt",
    "2 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "2 tablespoon butter",
    "455 gram cauliflower rice",
    "2 tablespoon soy sauce",
    "1 tablespoon garlic powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon onion powder",
    "salt and pepper (To taste)",
    "4 tablespoon full-fat plain greek yogurt",
    "2 tablespoon water",
    "2 teaspoon chili paste",
    "1 tablespoon sriracha",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "2 tablespoon full-fat plain greek yogurt",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, mix the ground beef and shawarma beef spices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate container, combine yogurt and lemon juice (from beef ingredient list) until homogeneous.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine beef and yogurt mixtures and mix until thoroughly combined and sticky. Set aside in the refrigerator while preparing the sauces.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "For the white garlic sauce, combine all white sauce ingredients in a container. Whisk to combine. Add more (or less) water for desired consistency. Transfer to a squeeze bottle or small mason jar. May be refrigerated up to two weeks.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "For the red pepper sauce, mix together all of the ingredients for the red sauce. Add more (or less) water for desired consistency. Transfer to a squeeze bottle or small mason jar. May be refrigerated up to two weeks.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat butter in a pan. Add marinated ground beef and saute until cooked through. Transfer to a bowl and cover with foil to keep warm.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "For cauliflower rice: using the same pan, add riced cauliflower. Mix in the soy sauce (from cauliflower rice ingredient list). Keep stirring until almost dry.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/shawarma-bowl-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "To assemble, layer cauliflower rice, beef, optional toppings, and sauces.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-shawarma/#wprm-recipe-52523-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
